  "summary": "The Blogspot Scene was an online-driven music scene that emerged in the early 2000s through members of the American post-noise underground.",
  "description": "The Blogspot Scene was an online-driven music scene that emerged in the early 2000s through members of the American post-noise underground. The style was associated with a distinct visual aesthetic, often featuring surrealist and psychedelic printed collage artwork on Dr/Am CDs and cassettes. Releases were made on independent net labels such as New Age Tapes, Pacific City Sound Visions, Housecraft Recordings and Ekhein.",
